  "writtenAt": "2026-10-31T13:23:52Z",
  "rule": "Fresh panel, seed 20261101, 20 pairs in 3 tiers, all endpoints restricted to the 159,129 MEASURED non-stop genotypes; every pair has Hamming(start,target)>=2 and score(target)>score(start). Tier 1 'seeded_initial' (pairs 0-6): mirrors their family-A rule under a different seed base - draw 96 random measured genotypes as the episode's initial observations, target = highest-scoring of those 96, start = uniformly random other member of those 96 with lower score and Hamming>=2 (uses only that episode's own initial-set labels). Tier 2 'random_uphill' (pairs 7-13): start and target drawn uniformly at random over all measured genotypes, resampled until Hamming>=2 and s[target]>s[start] (global score order only, never reachability). Tier 3 'parent_fresh' (pairs 14-19): start = published parent VFVS, target drawn uniformly from the 200 highest-scoring measured genotypes EXCLUDING their four published targets AIKG/CLKG/VLKG/ALKG - this tier is the direct probe of whether their VFVS->ALKG concentration is about the VFVS start or about those specific published targets. Difficulty guesses (tier 1 easier, tier 3 harder) are a priori and were not verified before the run. Each pair's 96 initial observations are drawn from its own sub-stream and are IDENTICAL across the five policies, as in their protocol.",
